 "_doc": "Talos (Argonautica 4.1638-1688; Apollodorus 1.9.26): the bronze giant who guarded Crete, running round it three times a day and hurling rocks at ships; one vein ran from his neck to his ankle, stopped by a bronze nail. A huge, heavily muscled man of bronze, short curled hair, blank glowing eyes, the vein running down him to the nail in his ankle; red-hot when he heats himself. Here, red-hot. Built by tools/art/build_gears.py.",
